From 6d6aa3345c9e2af191658a4120298098975e276d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 03:29:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 62/70] demux: xa: say how long each block is

The demuxer reads a fixed number of frames at a time and advances its
date by however many it got, so the last read - short of a full block
whenever the data does not divide by it - is dated correctly but says
nothing about how far it reaches. A reader left to guess that from the
block before it puts the end of the stream up to a block too late, which
on a repeat in place is silence the output has to invent at every loop.

Set the length from the increment the date accumulator has just been
given, which is the same number the samples were counted with.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/xa.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/xa.c b/modules/demux/xa.c
index a74adffc5f..3893e60a13 100644
--- a/modules/demux/xa.c
+++ b/modules/demux/xa.c
@@ -187,11 +187,17 @@ static int Demux( demux_t *p_demux )
 
     i_frames = p_block->i_buffer / p_sys->i_frame_size;
     p_block->i_dts = p_block->i_pts = date_Get( &p_sys->pts );
+    p_block->i_nb_samples = i_frames * FRAME_LENGTH;
+
+    /* The last read is short of a full block whenever the data does not
+     * divide by it, so say how far this one reaches rather than leave it to
+     * be guessed from the one before. */
+    p_block->i_length = date_Increment( &p_sys->pts, p_block->i_nb_samples )
+                      - p_block->i_dts;
+
     es_out_SetPCR( p_demux->out, p_block->i_pts );
     es_out_Send( p_demux->out, p_sys->p_es, p_block );
 
-    date_Increment( &p_sys->pts, i_frames * FRAME_LENGTH );
-
     return 1;
 }
 
